{"id":7881,"date":"2021-09-28T16:01:36","date_gmt":"2021-09-28T20:01:36","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?p=7881"},"modified":"2021-09-29T10:23:15","modified_gmt":"2021-09-29T14:23:15","slug":"montana-and-south-to-medora-and-beyond","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2021\/09\/28\/montana-and-south-to-medora-and-beyond\/","title":{"rendered":"Montana and South to Medora and Beyond"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>After Spearfish South Dakota and then our trip up to Fort Peck Montana to visit Ranger Scott and Ranger Sue, we came back down U.S. 85 into Medora North Dakota for a night.  We had been to Teddy Roosevelt National Park a couple years ago, so we didn&#8217;t take the time to drive through the park and all we did was walk to dinner from the campground and then did a little sightseeing as we walked through town on our way back to the campground.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2020\/11\/18\/really-unlimited-streaming-for-only-25-mo\/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210912_1646068372565837123502901033.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-7877\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210912_1646068372565837123502901033.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210912_1646068372565837123502901033-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210912_1646068372565837123502901033-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><\/a><figcaption>Kathy&#8217;s Strawberry Jalepino Margarita<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210912_1641404116869599675664832703.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-7878\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210912_1641404116869599675664832703.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210912_1641404116869599675664832703-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210912_1641404116869599675664832703-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><figcaption>Food prices seem high out here ($14 for a burger?)<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210912_172657300_hdr1312010386266594947.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-7876\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210912_172657300_hdr1312010386266594947.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210912_172657300_hdr1312010386266594947-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210912_172657300_hdr1312010386266594947-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><figcaption>Our after dinner walk in downtown Medora ND<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210912_1731075166639557663454861557.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-7879\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210912_1731075166639557663454861557.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210912_1731075166639557663454861557-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210912_1731075166639557663454861557-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><figcaption>More downtown Medora<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The next day we continued on down 85 for another nights stay in Spearfish on our way to Hot Springs.  Besides, we needed to check in at the Spearfish post office to see if our General Delivery package had arrived yet.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>This time instead of staying at a campground, we decided to take advantage of our <a href=\"https:\/\/harvesthosts.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Harvest Hosts<\/a> membership once again.  We reached out to<a href=\"https:\/\/mcguiganfarmexperience.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"> McGuigan Farm Experience<\/a> on the HH web site and they accepted our request to stay within just a couple hours.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Our host Nancy greeted us at the drive and welcomed us with a big smile and a little conversation.  She showed us where we could park.  It was a nice big hard packed grassy field that allowed us to pull straight in with our toad attached and was large enough we could just circle around in the morning to leave without ever having to unhook the toad.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_153247117388560929969083914.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-7882\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_153247117388560929969083914.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_153247117388560929969083914-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_153247117388560929969083914-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><figcaption>We had the place to ourselves<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>After we got settled in, Nancy took us on a tour of the farm.  Although it&#8217;s been in Mike&#8217;s family for generations and had been a working dairy farm for the vast majority of that time, they now rely on income from grain production and leasing out some of the land.  They have recently started the <a href=\"https:\/\/mcguiganfarmexperience.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">McGuigan Farm Experience<\/a> project to offer both school groups and the general public alike the opportunity to visit a real farm with real animals so that folks might learn about what a farmer really does and where that food on the table comes from.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\"><ul class=\"blocks-gallery-grid\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1605074146364160347079817186.jpg\" data-id=\"7886\" class=\"wp-image-7886\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1605074146364160347079817186.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1605074146364160347079817186-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1605074146364160347079817186-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><\/figure><\/li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1605026904325273499275326225.jpg\" data-id=\"7885\" class=\"wp-image-7885\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1605026904325273499275326225.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1605026904325273499275326225-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1605026904325273499275326225-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><\/figure><\/li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1859473682802670880974713656.jpg\" data-id=\"7883\" class=\"wp-image-7883\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1859473682802670880974713656.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1859473682802670880974713656-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1859473682802670880974713656-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><\/figure><\/li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1616476776266364512196030953.jpg\" data-id=\"7884\" class=\"wp-image-7884\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1616476776266364512196030953.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1616476776266364512196030953-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1616476776266364512196030953-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><\/figure><\/li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1605122618036960022053326800.jpg\" data-id=\"7887\" class=\"wp-image-7887\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1605122618036960022053326800.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1605122618036960022053326800-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210913_1605122618036960022053326800-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><\/figure><\/li><\/ul><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Nancy excused herself and left us to relax the rest of the evening and relaxing it was!  It was SO dark and SO quiet!  We had a wonderful nights sleep with the windows wide open and enjoyed a gentle breeze rolling over the hayfields that lulled us to sleep.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>As we prepared to depart in the morning, I noticed some water on the hardpack under the fresh water tank compartment.  Further inspection revealed that now the FRESH water tank fill hose had a small leak.  I figured it wasn&#8217;t hard to fix, (tighten a hose clamp), but this old body just doesn&#8217;t want to twist, turn, and stretch like this project would require.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Thankfully, we were at Spearfish which is just down the road from Belle Fourche which is the home of my new best (RV repairman) friend Jim and Progress RV.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>We didn&#8217;t even call ahead.  We left the farm and drove on up the ten minutes to see Jim in hopes he would drop whatever he was doing and come on over and take care of us.  And he did just that!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery columns-2 is-cropped wp-block-gallery-2 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\"><ul class=\"blocks-gallery-grid\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210907_1536014438232545177075051494.jpg\" data-id=\"7888\" class=\"wp-image-7888\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210907_1536014438232545177075051494.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210907_1536014438232545177075051494-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210907_1536014438232545177075051494-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><\/figure><\/li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210907_1326209591107994223343393724.jpg\" data-id=\"7889\" class=\"wp-image-7889\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210907_1326209591107994223343393724.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210907_1326209591107994223343393724-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/img_20210907_1326209591107994223343393724-685x514.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><\/figure><\/li><\/ul><figcaption class=\"blocks-gallery-caption\">My new Best Friend Jim @ Progress RV<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Next stop &#8230; Hot Springs South Dakota.  But first &#8211; the car goes in the shop for some unexpected repairs.  More on that in my next post.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Thanks for riding along.  You can leave any comments below.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Herb &amp; Kathy<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>After Spearfish South Dakota and then our trip up to Fort Peck Montana to visit Ranger Scott and Ranger Sue, we came back down U.S. 85 into Medora North Dakota for a night. We had been to Teddy Roosevelt National Park a couple years ago, so we didn&#8217;t take the time to drive through the &hellip; <a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2021\/09\/28\/montana-and-south-to-medora-and-beyond\/\" class=\"more-link\">Continue reading <span class=\"screen-reader-text\">Montana and South to Medora and Beyond<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[13403,18285,554707999,19546,554707329],"tags":[554708014,554707633,554708017,554707815,554708016,554707701,554708013,554707576,554707993,554708015,554707696,554707770],"class_list":["post-7881","post","type-post","status-publish","fo